From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: omap: veto OMAP4 idle while a wake-enabled level IRQ is asserted

With cpuidle C2 armed on a Nexus Q (OMAP4460, CPUs OFF, MPU in CSWR), the
BCM4330 WLAN -- SDIO with an out-of-band host-wake on gpio_53, level-high --
lost 4-26 % of pings in bursts of up to 29 s. Without C2: 0 %. With the MPU
held ON: 0.3 %. And a 20 Hz loop that merely read GPIO2's registers made
the loss vanish, while the same loop reading only /proc/interrupts made it
worse.

A level line that stays asserted after its interrupt was serviced (the chip
has more data) is not latched again while the bank smart-idles, because an
idle bank only reports edges. Once the MPU is in retention nothing keeps
GPIO2 awake, so the CPUs sleep through the line until an unrelated event
wakes the bank -- or a register access does.

Mainline only idles/checks banks on CPU_CLUSTER_PM_ENTER, which OMAP4
cpuidle issues only when MPU logic is lost (C3), and there it tests
IRQSTATUS: the very latch that is missing. Stock 3.0.8 ran
omap2_gpio_prepare_for_idle() before every deep entry (C2, C3, C4 and
suspend, 0xc0066428) and aborted the entry with -EBUSY if any wake-enabled
level line was at its active level on DATAIN (0xc021cbe0-cc10).

Do the same on CPU_PM_ENTER, on CPU0 only -- OMAP4's coupled idle powers
CPU0 down last, after CPU1 is OFF, which is where stock ran its hook; the
previous patch makes cpuidle44xx wake CPU1 after such a veto. Reading DATAIN
also wakes the bank, so the asserted level is latched and its interrupt
taken as soon as the veto returns. Limited to OMAP4 machines: AM33xx and
DRA7 share the "ti,omap4-gpio" register layout but not this idle path.

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-omap.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-omap.c
index 8693544..4f32ba9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-omap.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-omap.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <linux/gpio/driver.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <linux/platform_data/gpio-omap.h>
+#include <linux/smp.h>
 
 #define OMAP4_GPIO_DEBOUNCINGTIME_MASK 0xFF
 
@@ -71,6 +72,7 @@ struct gpio_bank {
 	bool dbck_flag;
 	bool loses_context;
 	bool context_valid;
+	bool level_wake_veto;
 	int stride;
 	u32 width;
 	int context_loss_count;
@@ -1276,6 +1278,27 @@ static void omap_gpio_unidle(struct gpio_bank *bank)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A level-triggered GPIO interrupt that is asserted but not latched in
+ * IRQSTATUS -- the line stayed at its active level after the previous
+ * interrupt was serviced, e.g. a WLAN host-wake with more data pending -- is
+ * not re-detected while the module smart-idles: an idle bank only reports
+ * edges. On OMAP4 the bank idles as soon as the MPU enters retention (cpuidle
+ * C2), so the CPUs would sleep through the line until something unrelated
+ * woke the bank; a BCM4330 over SDIO lost 4-26 % of pings in multi-second
+ * bursts that way. Stock OMAP4 kernels checked DATAIN against the wake-enabled
+ * level lines before every deep idle entry and aborted it with -EBUSY
+ * (omap2_gpio_prepare_for_idle()); do the same from CPU_PM_ENTER.
+ */
+static bool omap_gpio_level_wake_pending(struct gpio_bank *bank)
+{
+	u32 datain = readl_relaxed(bank->base + bank->regs->datain);
+	u32 active = (datain & bank->context.leveldetect1) |
+		     (~datain & bank->context.leveldetect0);
+
+	return active & bank->context.irqenable1 & bank->context.wake_en;
+}
+
 static int gpio_omap_cpu_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
 				  unsigned long cmd, void *v)
 {
@@ -1291,6 +1314,16 @@ static int gpio_omap_cpu_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
 		goto out_unlock;
 
 	switch (cmd) {
+	case CPU_PM_ENTER:
+		/*
+		 * OMAP4's coupled idle has CPU0 power down last, after CPU1 is
+		 * OFF: that is the moment the MPU (and with it this bank) may
+		 * idle, and a veto there is handled by cpuidle44xx.
+		 */
+		if (bank->level_wake_veto && smp_processor_id() == 0 &&
+		    omap_gpio_level_wake_pending(bank))
+			ret = NOTIFY_BAD;
+		break;
 	case CPU_CLUSTER_PM_ENTER:
 		mask = omap_get_gpio_irqbank_mask(bank);
 		isr = readl_relaxed(bank->base + bank->regs->irqstatus) & mask;
@@ -1433,6 +1466,11 @@ static int omap_gpio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (node) {
 		if (!of_property_read_bool(node, "ti,gpio-always-on"))
 			bank->loses_context = true;
+		/*
+		 * Not the whole "ti,omap4-gpio" family: AM33xx and DRA7 share the
+		 * register layout but not OMAP4's coupled idle.
+		 */
+		bank->level_wake_veto = of_machine_is_compatible("ti,omap4");
 	} else {
 		bank->loses_context = pdata->loses_context;
 
